<title>ISRAEL: M-Systems to buy Taiwan's C-One.</title>
<headline>M-Systems to buy Taiwan's C-One.</headline>
<dateline>TEL-AVIV, Israel 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>M-Systems Flash Disk Pioneers Ltd said it had signed a letter of intent to acquire Taiwan's C-One Technology and its U.S. subsidiary,  Pretec Electronics Corp, in exchange for 1.163 million shares of M-Systems.  </p>
<p>M-Systems' stock was trading at 7-3/8 in early trading Monday against 7-13/16 at the close on Friday.</p>
<p>C-One Technology designs, manufactures and markets PC Card solutions and Pretec Electronics Corp is its U.S. subsidiary, it said.</p>
<p>Combined revenues for the two companies totaled some $10 million and a net profit of $500,000, it said.</p>
<p>M-Systems makes software and hardware data storage solutions.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
